blem fits an appropriate inhaled ipratropium order?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Bronchospasm in selected obstructive-airway disease","explanation":"Ipratropium provides inhaled antimuscarinic bronchodilation in COPD and certain acute asthma regimens."},{"id":"B","text":"Cardiogenic pulmonary edema without bronchospasm","explanation":"An antimuscarinic bronchodilator does not resolve hydrostatic pulmonary edema."},{"id":"C","text":"Upper-airway stridor from a fixed obstruction","explanation":"Ipratropium does not remove a fixed upper-airway obstruction."},{"id":"D","text":"Pleural effusion with lung compression and no airflow obstruction","explanation":"Ipratropium cannot directly drain or resolve a pleural effusion."}],"answerKey":"A","point":"Identify the main treatment role taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-ipratropium--comprehensive--treatment-role","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-ipratropium::treatment-role"],"revision":"drug-dependent-20261106","sourceFields":["use"]},{"stem":"Which reassessment best evaluates the intended respiratory effect of AEROVENT — ipratropium bromide?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"INR, bruising, and puncture-site bleeding","explanation":"These assess an anticoagulation domain."},{"id":"B","text":"Bowel pattern, abdominal girth, and stool consistency","explanation":"These do not establish an airway treatment response."},{"id":"C","text":"Distal sensation, capillary refill, and cast tightness","explanation":"These assess a limb-safety domain."},{"id":"D","text":"Work of breathing, wheeze, RR, and SpO2","explanation":"These assess the patient’s response to bronchodilation."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Evaluate bronchodilation using breathing and oxygenation.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-ipratropium--comprehensive--bronchodilator_response","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-ipratropium::bronchodilator_response"],"answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"Which pair of effects is consistent with the an