umulation in renal impairment can increase seizure risk.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-pethidine--comprehensive--meperidine_renal","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-pethidine::meperidine_renal"],"answerKey":"B"}],"questionCount":7,"correctionRevision":"drug-dependent-20261106","model":"comprehensive-v1"}],"bankVersion":6,"legacyBankVersion":4,"sources":[{"id":"content-v35"},{"id":"label-ccu-pethidine","title":"MEPERIDINE HYDROCHLORIDE INJECTION [HIKMA PHARMACEUTICALS USA INC.]","url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=e0e998da-f056-4fce-be8e-ed60cf3b461b"}],"sourceFields":{"drugclass":"Opioid analgesic.","mechanism":"Mu-opioid receptor agonism produces analgesia and respiratory/CNS depression.","use":"Physician-prescribed analgesia for selected severe pain situations; not a routine first-choice treatment for every CCU chest-pain patient.","administration":"IM, SC or IV according to the product/order. If IV use is necessary, give very slowly per product labeling, preferably diluted, with monitoring and naloxone/assisted ventilation immediately available. Do not convert ampoule content into a default patient dose.","monitor":"• Check pain, sedation, RR, SpO2 and BP before/after. • Stop/escalate if breathing or consciousness deteriorates. • Nausea, vomiting, dizziness, sedation and hypotension can occur. • Avoid routine/repeated use with renal impairment because normeperidine can accumulate and increase seizure risk. • Review MAO inhibitors and serotonergic/CNS-depressant medicines. • Follow controlled-drug documentation/waste policy.","why":"Opioid respiratory depression is the immediate danger; normeperidine accumulation adds a distinctive seizure risk.","availability":"YES. Palestinian essential-medicine data list pethidine injection in 50- and 100-mg ampoules; verify concentration and route."},"readingSections":[{"field":"drugclass","label":"Drug class","text":"Opioid analgesic.","id":"section-0-62915714f176daff"},{"field":"mechanism","label":"Mechanism of action","text":"Mu-opioid receptor agonism produces analgesia and respiratory/CNS depression.","id":"section-1-3d319036a8e7e47e"},{"field":"use","label":"Main use","text":"Physician-prescribed analgesia for selected severe pain situations; not a routine first-choice treatment for every CCU chest-pain patient.","id":"section-2-69baf3207533de82"},{"field":"administration","label":"Form & administration","text":"IM, SC or IV according to the product/order. If IV use is necessary, give very slowly per product labeling, preferably diluted, with monitoring and naloxone/assisted ventilation immediately available. Do not convert ampoule content into a default patient dose.","id":"section-3-c8c76f72d3be83e1"},{"field":"monitor","label":"Nursing considerations","text":"• Check pain, sedation, RR, SpO2 and BP before/after. • Stop/escalate if breathing or consciousness deteriorates. • Nausea, vomiting, dizziness, sedation and hypotension can occur. • Avoid routine/repeated use with renal impairment because normeperidine can accumulate and increase seizure risk. • Review MAO inhibitors and serotonergic/CNS-depressant medicines. • Follow controlled-drug documentation/waste policy.","id":"section-4-f01e7119b7088495"},{"field":"why","label":"Essential rationale","text":"Opioid respiratory depression is the immediate danger; normeperidine accumulation adds a distinctive seizure risk.","id":"section-5-a725c84c9bc56f6a"},{"field":"availability","label":"Palestine availability","text":"YES. Palestinian essential-medicine data list pethidine injection in 50- and 100-mg ampoules; verify concentration and route.","id":"section-6-a08583ee82e79737"}],"legacyExams":[{"id":"ccu-pethidine--standard","itemId":"ccu-pethidine","itemType":"medication","title":"PETHIDINE — meperidine","stage":"standard","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"operator":">=","percent":90,"roundBeforeComparison":false},"timing":{"timed":false,"secondsPerQuestion":null,"timerEnforcement":