 treatment.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-pethidine--standard--hypotension","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-pethidine::hypotension"],"answerKey":"C"},{"stem":"After PETHIDINE — meperidine, which syndrome best explains agitation, fever, hyperreflexia, and autonomic instability?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Serotonin toxicity","explanation":"The combination of neuromuscular excitation and autonomic changes fits."},{"id":"B","text":"Vancomycin infusion intolerance","explanation":"This is a different administration-related reaction."},{"id":"C","text":"Isolated antimuscarinic intolerance","explanation":"This does not best explain the hyperreflexic serotonergic pattern."},{"id":"D","text":"Opioid respiratory toxicity","explanation":"This more typically produces depressed breathing and consciousness."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Recognize serotonin toxicity and review serotonergic combinations.","criticalForSafety":true,"id":"ccu-pethidine--standard--serotonin","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-pethidine::serotonin"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"A PETHIDINE — meperidine injection order is valid, but the minimum administration time is unclear. Which source should resolve preparation and rate?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"The instructions for a similar-looking vial on the trolley","explanation":"Appearance does not establish an equivalent product or rate."},{"id":"B","text":"The instructions for an oral product of the same name","explanation":"Oral instructions do not establish an IV administration rate."},{"id":"C","text":"The IV rate previously used for a different drug class","explanation":"Another drug’s administration rate is not transferable."},{"id":"D","text":"The exact product instructions and authorized local protocol","explanation":"Concentration, formulation, and indication can change administration requirements."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"IV administration speed follows the exact product and indication.","criticalForSafet