iated cardiac arrest. Use mainly for selected reversible causes/special circumstances such as specific toxicologic/metabolic indications.","id":"section-2-58bed618c4760ecd"},{"field":"administration","label":"Form & administration","text":"IV. The adult 8.4% emergency formulation is highly concentrated. Do not convert percentage, mL and mEq from memory; administration/dilution depend on the indication and actual product/protocol.","id":"section-3-79560bd5723f47e6"},{"field":"monitor","label":"Nursing considerations","text":"• Verify indication, concentration and ordered mEq. • Follow sodium, pH/ABG or VBG and potassium when indicated. • Excess can cause alkalemia, hypernatremia and sodium/volume load. • Do not improvise Y-site mixing with emergency drugs unless compatibility is confirmed. • It never substitutes for high-quality CPR/defibrillation/ventilation or treatment of the cause.","id":"section-4-9bac17d6925d3d81"},{"field":"why","label":"Essential rationale","text":"It changes acid-base chemistry; without a specific indication it can add sodium/alkali without fixing the cause.","id":"section-5-d44e60015754c237"},{"field":"availability","label":"Palestine availability","text":"YES. Palestinian MoH essential-medicine data document sodium bicarbonate 8.4% injection; container volume can vary.","id":"section-6-fa4035325ecfc8e5"}],"legacyExams":[{"id":"trolley-sodium-bicarbonate--standard","itemId":"trolley-sodium-bicarbonate","itemType":"medication","title":"SODIUM BICARBONATE","stage":"standard","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"operator":">=","percent":90,"roundBeforeComparison":false},"timing":{"timed":false,"secondsPerQuestion":null,"timerEnforcement":"persisted total deadline: 90 seconds multiplied by question count"},"scoring":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0,"unanswered":0,"partialCredit":false,"unsureOrGuessed":"review flag only","criticalSafetyMiss":"separate follow-up required; original numeric score unchanged"},"feedback":"show keys and all option